# Everything needs the owner's review.
#
# Paired with the "main: pull requests only" ruleset, which requires a code
# owner's approval before a pull request can merge. Without a file naming an
# owner that rule has nobody to ask and passes vacuously, so this is the half
# that gives it teeth.
#
# Only read from the default branch, so editing it on a side branch changes
# nothing until that branch lands.
#
# The repository-admin role bypasses the ruleset, which is deliberate: this
# gates contributions, and the owner is the reviewer rather than the reviewed.
# `make release` therefore pushes main directly and GitHub reports a bypassed
# rule violation on every release. That line is the arrangement working, not
# failing.
